Goldens for tests/pywheel/run.sh.

They were written by `tests/pywheel/run.sh --update` from the Flow tool and
checked against the Python generator (src/flow/python_generator.py through
`python3 -m flow.transpiler --python`) before it was deleted. Stdout, exit
status and every generated file matched byte for byte for all 17 cases, and
setup.py and pyproject.toml matched generate_setup_py and
generate_pyproject_toml.

Three stderr files carry the Flow tool's own message, by design:

  structs    The Python generator stopped on any public struct with fields
             with a traceback ("cannot unpack non-iterable Parameter
             object"). The tool stops at the same point with the same exit
             status and names the struct.
  typeerr    Type errors come from flowc's type checker (--strict) instead
             of the Python one.
  syntaxerr  Parse errors come from the flowc parser.

mathlib-wheel: the Python generator passed a relative `-w dist` to
`pip wheel` from a temporary directory, so a successful build left the wheel
behind and it reported "No wheel file produced". The driver passes the
absolute dist/ path. The golden covers the failed-build fallback, which both
print the same way.
